<title>ITALY: Italian crude imports fell 3.4 percent Jan-April.</title>
<headline>Italian crude imports fell 3.4 percent Jan-April.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian imports of crude oil fell 3.4 percent to some 24 million tonnes in the first four months of 1997 over the same period in 1996, trade body Unione Petrolifera (UP) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Libya accounted for 31.1 percent of imports, Saudi Arabia 18.3 percent, Iran 14.0 percent and the former Soviet Union 10.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
